WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:05.500
Last time we left Mexico it was in an ideological
struggle between the conservatives which favored

00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:10.889
a very centralized administration that retained
many aspects of the former colony with most

00:00:10.889 --> 00:00:16.299
favoring the reinstatement of a European style
Monarchy, and the liberals which favored curbing

00:00:16.299 --> 00:00:21.449
the power of the church and the military and
most wanting an establishment of a more USA

00:00:21.449 --> 00:00:22.590
style republic.

00:00:22.590 --> 00:00:28.039
And this ideological divide wouldn’t really
go away for the next century or more.

00:00:28.039 --> 00:00:32.559
Since Iturbide’s death Mexico was highly
unstable going from being an Empire to an

00:00:32.559 --> 00:00:36.850
ill-conceived republic to then being attacked
by Spain trying to requinquer it, to then

00:00:36.850 --> 00:00:41.710
another ill-conceived republic, to then losing
a war with Texas and the USA, while switching

00:00:41.710 --> 00:00:47.679
to a third ill-conceived republic, all while
this guy, Antonio López de Santa Anna a military

00:00:47.679 --> 00:00:52.609
leader/president/dictator kind of controlled
things to various degrees during this period.

00:00:52.609 --> 00:00:57.190
Ou and while all of this was happening a bunch
conservative and liberal rebellions occurred

00:00:57.190 --> 00:01:00.529
as well helping to increase the natural chaos
of the era.

00:01:00.529 --> 00:01:04.049
All of this combined and more that we don’t
have time to talk about meant that Mexico

00:01:04.049 --> 00:01:06.039
was in a deep state of shit ehh I mean poop.

00:01:06.039 --> 00:01:13.390
And it is this state of affairs in the year
of 1854 that we start our journey.

00:01:13.390 --> 00:01:17.429
As I have mentioned before since the first
Mexican Empire, the mexican politics were

00:01:17.429 --> 00:01:20.929
largely dictated by one person, Santa Anna.

00:01:20.929 --> 00:01:26.750
He is a complicated character to say the least,
he was a prominent military leader a president

00:01:26.750 --> 00:01:28.140
and a dictator.

00:01:28.140 --> 00:01:32.240
Sometimes all at once, sometimes one at a
time, sometimes he called politics boring

00:01:32.240 --> 00:01:36.460
and left on a military campaign while leaving
someone else in charge, sometimes he left

00:01:36.460 --> 00:01:40.890
completely only to later come back, it was
a game of hats to him.

00:01:40.890 --> 00:01:44.719
None the less even though it can’t be said
that he completely controlled Mexico during

00:01:44.719 --> 00:01:49.640
the entire time since the dissolution of the
Empire, he was so prominent in Mexican politics

00:01:49.640 --> 00:01:54.210
during this time that many historians just
call it “the age of Santa Anna” as all

00:01:54.210 --> 00:01:59.409
major events in Mexican history during this
era involved him in one way or another.

00:01:59.409 --> 00:02:03.619
He wasn’t really liked by the conservatives
or the liberals as his “reforms” were

00:02:03.619 --> 00:02:08.090
very staunchly centralist not giving either
side what they wanted.

00:02:08.090 --> 00:02:12.569
He mainly managed to stay in power because
of public support, political maneuvering between

00:02:12.569 --> 00:02:15.870
the two factions and the backing from the
military.

00:02:15.870 --> 00:02:21.480
But in 1854 he was finally overthrown by the
liberals, who quickly started implementing

00:02:21.480 --> 00:02:23.989
their laws known as La Reforma.

00:02:23.989 --> 00:02:28.790
Culminating in the 1857 new constitution,
which by the way if you’re keeping count

00:02:28.790 --> 00:02:31.290
is the 4th ill-conceived republic.

00:02:31.290 --> 00:02:36.451
Nonetheless the conservatives weren’t happy
to say the least, and with this new 1857 liberal

00:02:36.451 --> 00:02:39.379
constitution something had to be done.

00:02:39.379 --> 00:02:44.189
So they launched a Coup d'état, taking control
of Mexico City and rolling back the liberal

00:02:44.189 --> 00:02:45.189
reforms.

00:02:45.189 --> 00:02:50.349
The liberals retreated to Veracruz and called
the conservative government iligitmenet, and

00:02:50.349 --> 00:02:55.519
so the rest of Mexico had to choose whether
to support the Liberal government in Veracruz

00:02:55.519 --> 00:03:01.371
or the Conservative government in Mexico City
and with that the civil war known as the Reform

00:03:01.371 --> 00:03:02.940
War started.

00:03:02.940 --> 00:03:07.590
Initially the conservative forces head an
upper hand already controlling some of the

00:03:07.590 --> 00:03:12.709
Liberal states and having a much better equipped
and trained army, however USA decided it would

00:03:12.709 --> 00:03:18.360
be better for them if Mexico was controlled
by the republic leaning liberals rather than

00:03:18.360 --> 00:03:23.269
monarchy leaning conservatives, and so they
started to support the liberals, who in the

00:03:23.269 --> 00:03:28.910
end thanks in part to this support managed
to win in 1860 appointing Benito Juárez as

00:03:28.910 --> 00:03:31.969
the new Meixcan president in 1861.

00:03:31.969 --> 00:03:35.640
But at this point as you would imagine, Mexico
was devastated.

00:03:35.640 --> 00:03:41.400
It’s infrastructure in ruins, immensely
in debt, the economy barely holding together,

00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:45.731
and conservative gorillas still patrolling
the countryside trying to fight the liberal

00:03:45.731 --> 00:03:47.510
government wherever they can.

00:03:47.510 --> 00:03:52.810
Benito Juarez had no choice but to default
on the Mexican debt which was mainly owned

00:03:52.810 --> 00:03:55.519
by the British, French and Spanish.

00:03:55.519 --> 00:04:00.560
Obviously these three countries weren’t
happy with this and so decided to invade Mexico

00:04:00.560 --> 00:04:03.700
to force the liberal government to pay its
debt.

00:04:03.700 --> 00:04:07.110
But not all of these countries had the same
plan.

00:04:07.110 --> 00:04:12.060
Napoleon the 3rd king of France was hoping
to install a French favoring monarchy in Mexico

00:04:12.060 --> 00:04:14.670
as to have an ally in the new world.

00:04:14.670 --> 00:04:19.380
And when Mexico defaulted on its debt it gave
Napoleon the perfect causes belly to make

00:04:19.380 --> 00:04:24.530
this happen, plus USA was in the middle of
a civil war meaning they couldn’t interfere

00:04:24.530 --> 00:04:26.100
with Napoleon's plan.

00:04:26.100 --> 00:04:30.660
When the English and Spanish found out about
the ulterior plans of the French they promptly

00:04:30.660 --> 00:04:34.630
withdrew their forces as they didn’t want
to support a French coup.

00:04:34.630 --> 00:04:40.110
Now alone the French army was defeated on
May the 5th at the Battle of Puebla by Ignacio

00:04:40.110 --> 00:04:41.110
Zaragoza.

00:04:41.110 --> 00:04:46.440
This Mexican victory is celebrated today as
CInco de Mayo, which if you ask me is kind

00:04:46.440 --> 00:04:49.750
of a Random Battle to have a whole holiday
around.

00:04:49.750 --> 00:04:54.250
Yes the Mexicans won against a much better
trained and equipped French army all while

00:04:54.250 --> 00:04:59.321
being outnumbered 2 to 1, but in the grand
scheme of things the battle didn’t really

00:04:59.321 --> 00:05:00.600
change much.

00:05:00.600 --> 00:05:04.971
The French army just retreated, waited for
reinforcements and then defeated the Mexican

00:05:04.971 --> 00:05:06.280
army anyways.

00:05:06.280 --> 00:05:10.750
Yes there are some interesting aspects of
the battle applyed to it retroactively but

00:05:10.750 --> 00:05:15.370
during that time it was just another battle
of many in Mexican history.

00:05:15.370 --> 00:05:16.820
But I digress.

00:05:16.820 --> 00:05:19.440
Napoleon now controlled Mexico, well kind
of.

00:05:19.440 --> 00:05:24.780
The Liberal government of Benito Juarez relocated
to Chihuahua with the countries treasury,

00:05:24.780 --> 00:05:30.220
hoping to continue the fight against the French,
which they did but very unsuccessfully.

00:05:30.220 --> 00:05:34.210
Napoleon also gained support from the Mexican
conservatives whom ever since their lose in

00:05:34.210 --> 00:05:37.150
the Reform War wanted to get their power back.

00:05:37.150 --> 00:05:41.740
So with Mexico now largely in the French hands
and with the help of the conservatives the

00:05:41.740 --> 00:05:44.460
second Mexican Empire was declared.

00:05:44.460 --> 00:05:49.780
Not long after that a suitable European monarch
to take the new throne was searched for.

00:05:49.780 --> 00:05:55.500
Kind of having a dejavu here.

00:05:55.500 --> 00:06:01.740
A suitable monarch was quickly found, Austrian
born Ferdinand Maximilian Joseph from the

00:06:01.740 --> 00:06:08.140
house of Habsburg-Lorraine the younger brother
of Franze Joseph yes that Franz Joseph.

00:06:08.140 --> 00:06:13.520
But unlike his brother Maximilian was a true
renaissance man believing in the many ideas

00:06:13.520 --> 00:06:15.520
that came from the enlightenment.

00:06:15.520 --> 00:06:22.330
By age 17 he was taking 55 different classes
ranging from fencing to history and engineering,

00:06:22.330 --> 00:06:26.590
he also spoke 7 to 8 languages including Spanish.

00:06:26.590 --> 00:06:31.000
In everything Maximilian ever did, he was
trying to surpass his older brother, to show

00:06:31.000 --> 00:06:35.880
everyone that even though not in line for
the throne he would be a better ruler than

00:06:35.880 --> 00:06:36.970
Franz Joseph.

00:06:36.970 --> 00:06:41.470
In the end he was largely ignored and held
several royal positions within the Austrian

00:06:41.470 --> 00:06:47.280
kingdom before being asked by Napoleon the
3rd if he wanted the Mexican throne.

00:06:47.280 --> 00:06:51.340
Maximilian didn’t want to take the crown
at first saying he will only take it, if the

00:06:51.340 --> 00:06:54.000
Mexican people vote in favor of him.

00:06:54.000 --> 00:06:59.930
Napoleon along with the Mexican conservatives
obliged and staged a dubious vote which unsurprisingly

00:06:59.930 --> 00:07:04.080
turned out overwhelmingly in the favor of
Maximilian.

00:07:04.080 --> 00:07:08.460
Unbeknownst to the fabricated vote Maximilian
promptly left for Mexico with his wife Charlotte

00:07:08.460 --> 00:07:14.650
of Belgium, hoping to once and for all prove
to everyone that he will be a great monarch.

00:07:14.650 --> 00:07:16.850
Maximilian arrived to Mexico to a very cold
welcome.

00:07:16.850 --> 00:07:21.870
There wasn’t even anyone in Veracruz to
meet him, he just kind of stepped off the

00:07:21.870 --> 00:07:23.460
boat and waited.

00:07:23.460 --> 00:07:28.710
Turns out the conservative attache that was
supposed to meet Maximilian in Veracruz confused

00:07:28.710 --> 00:07:31.930
the time of his arrival and so came much later.

00:07:31.930 --> 00:07:36.330
Nonetheless Meximilian was taken to Mexico
City where he chose Chapultepec castle as

00:07:36.330 --> 00:07:37.740
his seat of power.

00:07:37.740 --> 00:07:43.640
But this is where the entire situation started
to become much more clearer to Meximilian.

00:07:43.640 --> 00:07:47.960
First he found out that he wasn’t actually
elected by the Mexican people and many of

00:07:47.960 --> 00:07:50.030
them didn’t want him here.

00:07:50.030 --> 00:07:54.550
Second he realized he was only in power, because
of the French military in Mexico that was

00:07:54.550 --> 00:07:56.210
keeping him in power.

00:07:56.210 --> 00:07:59.840
Without it the liberal government of Juarez
would come back.

00:07:59.840 --> 00:08:04.670
Third, turns out that Mexico was financial
in a disaster.

00:08:04.670 --> 00:08:08.800
This combined with the fact that a large portion
of the treasury was taken by the liberals

00:08:08.800 --> 00:08:14.050
and that it wasn’t him but the French government
who controlled the Mexican finance ministry,

00:08:14.050 --> 00:08:19.140
meant that even though Maximilian was the
emperor he did not have control over the country's

00:08:19.140 --> 00:08:22.520
coffers or the military keeping him in power.

00:08:22.520 --> 00:08:26.360
But that didn’t disway the young emperor
who had something to prove.

00:08:26.360 --> 00:08:31.900
He quickly got to work reforming the Mexican
Empire according to the ideas of the enlightenment,

00:08:31.900 --> 00:08:36.270
which by the way where very similar to the
ideas that the liberals implemented at the

00:08:36.270 --> 00:08:39.900
start of the reform war just a couple of years
back.

00:08:39.900 --> 00:08:45.279
Meximilian abolished the large haciendas’
monopolies in Mexico, restricted working hours,

00:08:45.279 --> 00:08:50.660
banned child labor, cancelled all pesents’
debt under 10 pesos, and banned all the selling

00:08:50.660 --> 00:08:55.960
and reselling of indebted Mexican peasents
known as peons, who up untill now where more

00:08:55.960 --> 00:08:57.149
like slaves.

00:08:57.149 --> 00:09:01.959
He enacted many more other liberal reforms
but we don’t have time to talk about all

00:09:01.959 --> 00:09:02.990
of them.

00:09:02.990 --> 00:09:08.250
Naturally all these liberal reforms started
to anger the conservatives who brought Maximilian

00:09:08.250 --> 00:09:12.389
here to get rid of the liberal reforms not
to pass them.

00:09:12.389 --> 00:09:17.439
However Maximilians wife known in Mexico as
Carlota through lavish Austrian style galas

00:09:17.439 --> 00:09:21.930
and parties to keep the aristocrats at least
somewhat occupied.

00:09:21.930 --> 00:09:28.360
Plus in the conservative minds having a liberal
monarch is still better than a liberal government.

00:09:28.360 --> 00:09:33.290
Meximilian also brought many Austrian engineers
to help build up the Mexican infrastructure

00:09:33.290 --> 00:09:38.360
and mainly rebuild Mexico city in the style
of the European capital cities.

00:09:38.360 --> 00:09:43.750
For example, today's famous Paseo de La Reforma
was built by Maximilian.

00:09:43.750 --> 00:09:46.569
Suddenly the tide started to change.

00:09:46.569 --> 00:09:52.870
Many liberals seeing Maximilian’s reforms
started to take up administrative jobs within

00:09:52.870 --> 00:09:57.420
Maximilian’s government, thinking maybe
having this emperor isn’t that bad.

00:09:57.420 --> 00:10:02.509
The peasants also started to turn to Meximilian’s
side mainly the indios class who saw having

00:10:02.509 --> 00:10:08.480
an emperor a much better option than being
controlled by a majority mestizo/criollo liberal

00:10:08.480 --> 00:10:09.480
government.

00:10:09.480 --> 00:10:14.170
And over all, even the people who didn’t
want a monarchy started to become much less

00:10:14.170 --> 00:10:19.829
vocal about it, as everyone was sick of fighting
at this point and if peace meant having an

00:10:19.829 --> 00:10:22.790
Austrian monarch so be it.

00:10:22.790 --> 00:10:27.329
Maximilian even tried to endear himself to
the Mexican people by walking around the capital

00:10:27.329 --> 00:10:33.540
with no guards or ontarouge wearing a Sombrero
and a Mexican charro, just chatting with the

00:10:33.540 --> 00:10:35.920
people and seeing how the day was going.

00:10:35.920 --> 00:10:41.440
He even offered Juarez a pardon and a prime
ministerial position in his new government.

00:10:41.440 --> 00:10:46.000
Juarez however declined, he didn’t fight
Santa Anna and then the reform war just to

00:10:46.000 --> 00:10:48.889
now work under a foreing monarch.

00:10:48.889 --> 00:10:52.769
And that is where the troubles for Maximlian
start piling on.

00:10:52.769 --> 00:10:58.310
The liberals were almost stomped out by the
French army but then the US civil war ended.

00:10:58.310 --> 00:11:02.690
USA now no longer preoccupied decided it was
time to intervene.

00:11:02.690 --> 00:11:06.579
The reasons for the intervention where mainly
that the US didn’t support the liberals

00:11:06.579 --> 00:11:11.910
in the reform wars just to see them now lose
power and also because all of this was a European

00:11:11.910 --> 00:11:17.569
intervention in the Americas, which under
the US Monroe Doctrine was a no go.

00:11:17.569 --> 00:11:21.070
Which seems kind of hypocritical but I digress.

00:11:21.070 --> 00:11:25.199
President Andrew Johnson couldn’t get the
congress to agree on an intervention plan,

00:11:25.199 --> 00:11:30.569
so he just relocated a lot of the US army
to the Mexcian Border and then just had them

00:11:30.569 --> 00:11:35.060
“lose their weapons and supply” somewhere
in that area.

00:11:35.060 --> 00:11:39.769
The Mexican liberals, now with US support
could finally go on the offencive and started

00:11:39.769 --> 00:11:42.970
to win a bunch of battles and retake some
land.

00:11:42.970 --> 00:11:49.019
Meximilian was now forced to enact the Balck
Decree which made anyone forming any armed

00:11:49.019 --> 00:11:53.710
bands to be imprisoned and executed within
twenty four hours.

00:11:53.710 --> 00:11:59.500
This did slow down the liberals but also angered
many other people who were appalled by all

00:11:59.500 --> 00:12:05.040
the killing, sometimes even of innocent people
who happened to have guns on them, so many

00:12:05.040 --> 00:12:07.809
people started to support the liberals again.

00:12:07.809 --> 00:12:13.040
While this was happening USA exerted a lot
of diplomatic pressure on France urging them

00:12:13.040 --> 00:12:19.059
to leave at once, this combined with a looming
Franco-Prussian war back in Europe, meant

00:12:19.059 --> 00:12:24.269
that Napoleon had no choice but to withdraw
all of his troops from Mexico.

00:12:24.269 --> 00:12:29.470
Without the French army the Mexcian Empire
would surely fall and Napoleon urged Maximilian

00:12:29.470 --> 00:12:30.959
to leave the country.

00:12:30.959 --> 00:12:36.139
But Maximilian ever the naive Emperor was
convinced by his conservative advisors that

00:12:36.139 --> 00:12:41.069
a solid defence can be mustered up against
the liberals even without the French.

00:12:41.069 --> 00:12:46.510
However unbeknownst to Maximilian the conservatives
didn’t have much power anymore ever since

00:12:46.510 --> 00:12:51.709
their defeat in the reform war and this proposed
defence was just a pipedream.

00:12:51.709 --> 00:12:56.990
As a last ditch effort Maximilian himself
went on to lead his troops in to battle, and

00:12:56.990 --> 00:13:02.459
when it became obvious that the Liberals will
win, he allegedly hoped for a “lucky bullet”

00:13:02.459 --> 00:13:07.350
that would kill him in battle fighting for
his country, but it never came and eventually

00:13:07.350 --> 00:13:09.930
he was captured and sentenced to death.

00:13:09.930 --> 00:13:15.449
A day before the execution Maximilian was
offered a chance to escape but he refused

00:13:15.449 --> 00:13:20.569
as his Mexican generals who were ordered to
be executed with him couldn’t make it and

00:13:20.569 --> 00:13:22.589
he wouldn’t leave them behind.

00:13:22.589 --> 00:13:27.730
Also escaping would mean shaving his beard
which along with the escape itself would taint

00:13:27.730 --> 00:13:33.339
his proud Habsburg heritage if caught, and
so he will stay and face the firing squad

00:13:33.339 --> 00:13:36.769
as an Emperor.

00:13:36.769 --> 00:13:40.750
His last words before a firing squad where
in flawless spanish.

00:13:40.750 --> 00:13:46.959
"I forgive everyone, and I ask everyone to
forgive me.

00:13:46.959 --> 00:13:53.439
May my blood, which is about to be shed, be
for the good of the country.

00:13:53.439 --> 00:14:01.220
Viva Mexico, viva la independencia!"

00:14:01.220 --> 00:14:07.339
Maximilian wasn’t a perfect monarch, he
was naive, easily swayed by other people and

00:14:07.339 --> 00:14:12.740
even though goal oriented he was very indecisive
on how to get to those goals.

00:14:12.740 --> 00:14:18.490
But with his liberal ideas and openness to
hear out his advisors, with his care for all

00:14:18.490 --> 00:14:24.860
people regardless of class and his passion
to improve the living standards for all Mexicans,

00:14:24.860 --> 00:14:28.950
he was in a way the perfect monarch for Mexico.

00:14:28.950 --> 00:14:34.999
And ironically while pursuing their goal to
stabilize the country, the liberals may have

00:14:34.999 --> 00:14:40.839
squandered the best chance for peace and stability,
Mexico had in a long time.

00:14:40.839 --> 00:14:46.250
Or maybe not, maybe the US would invade or
France would fully take over, who knows.

00:14:46.250 --> 00:14:51.949
However I will end with this statement, after
the reinstatement of the republican government

00:14:51.949 --> 00:14:58.029
Juarez thought about releasing a list of all
the liberals that asked for or gotten a job

00:14:58.029 --> 00:15:03.759
within the Maximilian administration, to which
Sebastián Lerdo a prominent liberal him self

00:15:03.759 --> 00:15:13.619
replied “If you publish that list, there
will no longer be a liberal party”.

00:15:13.619 --> 00:15:18.490
That is where this video ends, please do read
the description for so much more information

00:15:18.490 --> 00:15:23.029
that I was unable to cram in to this already
pretty long video.

00:15:23.029 --> 00:15:27.269
Information like the fact that there are several
contradicting sources on what the actual last

00:15:27.269 --> 00:15:31.990
words of Maximilian were, so if you want to
know what Maximilian may have said, check

00:15:31.990 --> 00:15:33.540
out the description.

